Scope of this fork
------------------
Only the MIT-licensed part of the upstream repository is included:
everything outside the directories listed below.

The following upstream directories are NOT MIT-licensed. They are governed by the
a separate proprietary license, which forbids copying, redistribution and
sublicensing, and requires a paid license for production use. They are therefore
deliberately excluded from this repository and must not be added to it:

  app/proprietary/
  app/saas/
  engine/
  frontend/src/processor/
  frontend/src/editor/proprietary/
  frontend/src/editor/desktop/
  frontend/src/editor/saas/
  frontend/src/editor/cloud/

Changes from upstream
---------------------
- Renamed and rebranded to "Kagaz PDF".
- Built permanently in upstream's "core" flavor (no :proprietary / :saas modules).
- Removed the upstream PostHog project key and the Scarf tracking pixel;
  analytics are disabled by default.
- Removed upstream release/CI infrastructure and the desktop (Tauri) shell,
  whose sources are part of the excluded proprietary directories.
- Added original implementations (Apache-2.0) of login/users, audit log,
  OpenID Connect SSO (app/auth) and an Electron desktop shell (desktop/).
  These were written without copying or consulting the proprietary sources.

Internal Java package names and some environment variable prefixes are
inherited from upstream and kept for compatibility.

Third-party components keep their own licenses; see
frontend/src/assets/3rdPartyLicenses.json and the Gradle dependency tree.
